TinyELF Basic is built on, and contains parts of, the following work
by other people.


Basic2 by Stefan Lenz
https://github.com/slviajero/tinybasic

  The BASIC interpreter: basic.h, hardware.h, language.h, runtime.h
  and the interpreter parts of main.c and runtime.c,
  licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 as stated
  in the source headers. Basic2 descends from Palo Alto Tiny BASIC
  by Li-Chen Wang (1976).


36-character display kernel by Omegamatrix
https://forums.atariage.com/topic/317204-36-character-kernel-redux

  The 36-column text display and its font, published on AtariAge.
  TinyELF Basic re-implements the kernel in C on the ARM (main.c).


AtariVox/SaveKey I2C driver (i2c_v2.3.inc)
by Alex Herbert (2004), optimisations by Thomas Jentzsch (2006/2008)

  i2c_savekey.c is a port of this 6507 driver to the ARM.


vcsLib by Zachary Scolaro
https://github.com/Al-Nafuur/United-Carts-of-Atari

  vcsLib.h is copied unchanged from the UCA firmware for the PlusCart
  and UnoCart, licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3.


Cephes Mathematical Library by Stephen L. Moshier
https://www.netlib.org/cephes/

  The polynomial coefficients of SIN, COS, TAN, ATAN, LOG and EXP in
  tinymath.c are taken from the single precision functions of Cephes
  (sinf, expf, logf, atanf), which "may be used freely".


